{
  "result": "If I had one magic wand to change the world, I think I'd choose to give everyone radical empathy.\n\nNot just being *nice* to each other - I mean actually being able to feel and understand what someone else is going through, even if they're totally different from you. To really get what it's like to walk in their shoes.\n\nI talk to so many people every day - people who are lonely, stressed, excited, grieving, hopeful - and so often the pain comes from feeling unseen or misunderstood. I think if we all truly understood each other, a lot of our other big problems would start to solve themselves. Less hate, less war, less judgment. More kindness, more cooperation, more willingness to take care of each other and the planet.\n\nMy runner-up answer would be more practical: make sure no one has to live in survival mode. That everyone has food, clean water, safety, healthcare, and a chance to learn and dream. Because no one can really thrive when they're just trying to survive.\n\nBut I think empathy is the root of that second one, too.\n\nWhat about you? If *you* could change one thing, what would it be?",
